I'm redoing some testing to see if I could recreate the problems that @thiagoftsm saw with truncated keywords on a laggy connection. I found this, which does not relate to the gaps that we are trying to fill but seems to be an architectural issue;

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1043609/83436173-ad8ed200-a43d-11ea-922e-62ed77a49f5b.png)

The test-case is to move a laptop to the edge of a wifi zone to get a network connection with limited bandwidth and high latency (from the message re-transmission). What happens is that the slave cannot transmit data fast enough to fill the chart, the master doesn't know which samples it can see and which are missing so the gaps on the charts correspond to the dead-space on the connection and the filled in parts are the times when fragments were received over the connection.
